      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1187572/how-surface-materials-shape-contemporary-interiors",
      "title": "How Surface Materials Shape Contemporary Interiors",
      "content_html": "<p>Whether in residential interiors, workplaces, hospitality environments, or public spaces, the relationship between aesthetic intentions and technical performance can redefine how surfaces are used and how they perform. A material selected for its specific color, texture, or finish must remain visually coherent when applied to furniture fronts, cabinetry, countertops, and other interior elements. Yet how can architects and designers create visually distinctive and tactilely engaging interiors while preserving their original design intentions across different applications?</p>",
